<!--
    Kuna #1028: a guarded relative jump table is read past its guard, into the
    table that follows it, and the extra rows send flow into the middle of
    instructions (halt_baddata).

    unrolled() reaches its dispatch block from two copies of the bound
    check, one per predecessor, with opposite branch senses (the shape of
    libselinux getprocattrcon_raw):

        movzx eax, byte ptr [rdi]      movzx eax, byte ptr [rdi+1]
        sub   eax, 0x63                sub   eax, 0x63
        cmp   al, 4                    cmp   al, 4
        ja    default                  jbe   dispatch
    dispatch:
        lea   rdx, [rip+table_u]; movzx eax, al
        movsxd rax, dword ptr [rdx+rax*4]; add rax, rdx; notrack jmp rax

    table_u (5 rows) is immediately followed by other relative tables.
    Upstream checkUnrolledGuard requires every copy to branch the same way,
    so no guard bounded the merged index, and its full byte range was read.

    Stage: P2 switch model (unrolled guard, JumpBasic::check_unrolled_guard).
    P0 assertion: option switchmultipred on|off.  With the option on (the
    default) each copy of the check is pulled back to its own MULTIEQUAL
    input and the merged index is bounded by the union of the ranges.

    Pass 1 (default) asserts the fix: the switch closes after 'g' (0x67).
    Pass 2 (switchmultipred off) asserts the bug: row 5 (0x68), past the
    guard, is read.
-->
